  "worked_solution": "We start with the ratio $6:5$ and write it as a fraction:\n\n$$\n\\frac{6}{5}\n$$\n\nIn this fraction, the numerator represents the number of peaches and the denominator represents the number of pears.\n\nWe can make a numerator of $60$ by multiplying the numerator and denominator by $10$:\n\n$$\n\\frac{6\\times 10}{5\\times 10}=\\frac{60}{50}\n$$\n\nTherefore, there are $50$ pears in Sophia's store.",
